<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manila galleon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1565">1565</a>–<a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galleon">galleon</a> was the Spanish trade route across the Pacific between Manila and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acapulco">Acapulco</a>, in operation from 1565 to 1815. Galleons carried American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and returned with Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> and other goods. The trade linked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and was one of the first sustained global trade routes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila-galleon.jpg" alt="Manila galleon" width="320" height="134" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA/JPL/NIMA; derivative work by Uxbona · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:16th_century_Portuguese_Spanish_trade_routes.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
